00:03:55,560 --> 00:04:00,200
And so in light of an election, I know that we have a diverse congregation.

72
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:05,420
And I don't know how you came in feeling this morning, but I know that if you consider yourself

73
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:10,680
a Christian, that your primary citizenship is in heaven.

74
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:17,480
And so what better two weeks to look at what the Bible says about heaven and what the Bible

75
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:22,100
says about Jesus' reign on heaven and earth than these next two weeks.

76
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:27,780
So let's lean in and let's think about the ways in which the way God rules heaven impacts

77
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:30,400
the way that we live our daily lives today.

78
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:33,840
See, as American Christians, I think, at least this is the way that I grew up, I don't know

79
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:39,700
about you, I tend to think about heaven as a distant place with mostly future implications

80
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:41,340
for my life.

81
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:46,300
But when we look at the Scriptures and when we really investigate what the Scriptures say

82
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:50,820
about heaven, we find out that heaven is actually a place that's much closer than we

83
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:55,880
realize, and I think it has massive implications for our everyday life.

84
00:04:55,880 --> 00:05:00,600
See, Christians tend to think about, I don't know, again, maybe I'm just bringing my baggage

85
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,100
to you all.

86
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:04,420
We tend to think about heaven as a place we go when we die.

87
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:09,580
But when the Bible talks about heaven, heaven is the place where God dwells.

88
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:14,680
And so in theory, by connection, right?

89
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:17,780
To be absent with the bodies, to be present with the Lord.

90
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:19,560
So heaven is where we go when we die.

91
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:22,720
But it's not, that's not the primary focus of heaven in the Bible.

92
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:28,700
The primary focus of heaven in the Bible is the one who dwells there eternally, God.

93
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:30,940
So that's what heaven is all about.

94
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:32,760
And that's my message.

95
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:33,400
So let's go home.

