00:31:36,540 --> 00:31:43,600
That this is how God has always operated, that he has always dealt with sin with both justice and mercy.

433
00:31:43,600 --> 00:31:49,620
That he extends grace and forgiveness to those who would have eyes to see, who would receive it as a free gift.

434
00:31:49,620 --> 00:31:55,940
The God who was and is to come is dealing with sin, both with justice and mercy.

435
00:31:57,080 --> 00:31:59,300
Around the throne are 24 thrones.

436
00:31:59,300 --> 00:32:02,300
Again, numbers, images, they would have understood it.

437
00:32:02,300 --> 00:32:04,060
24 divided by 2 is 12.

438
00:32:04,060 --> 00:32:07,760
We have the 12 tribes of Israel and the 12 apostles of the church.

439
00:32:07,760 --> 00:32:16,520
This is meant to remind us that God, as he's dealing with sin, he is always in partnership with human beings to bring about his mercy to the world.

440
00:32:16,520 --> 00:32:18,880
He partnered with Israel in the Old Testament.

441
00:32:18,880 --> 00:32:20,680
He's partnering with the church in the New Testament.

442
00:32:20,680 --> 00:32:26,120
God is, was, and always will work through human partnerships to bring about his mercy and his justice.

443
00:32:27,080 --> 00:32:29,780
Then we see four living creatures, which have eyes all over.

444
00:32:29,780 --> 00:32:30,920
That's a fun one.

445
00:32:30,920 --> 00:32:33,500
If you ever see somebody try and draw that, really fun.

446
00:32:33,500 --> 00:32:37,580
Four is a number of wholeness in the Bible.

447
00:32:37,580 --> 00:32:40,980
And the, the, the beasts have certain faces.

448
00:32:40,980 --> 00:32:50,420
And essentially the, the symbolism there is to, to symbolize, that's the word I was looking for, the totality of creation.

449
00:32:51,020 --> 00:32:52,180
All of creation.

450
00:32:52,180 --> 00:32:56,800
So here's the main point of chapter, of verses three through seven.

451
00:32:56,800 --> 00:32:58,900
In my opinion, again, I'm not an expert.

452
00:32:58,900 --> 00:33:01,560
Please test this with your own theories.

453
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:03,200
But I would say this on your bulletin.

454
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:10,100
God was, is, and will redeem humanity to himself and restore creation to its intended design.

455
00:33:10,100 --> 00:33:19,220
Verses three through seven show us around the throne of God that God is working with humanity to bring about redemption for humans and restoration of all creation.

456
00:33:19,220 --> 00:33:29,280
These are images that on the surface look a little bit scary and confusing to us, but they're actually intended us, intended to remind us of God's eternal character.

457
00:33:29,280 --> 00:33:35,180
That he has a plan to redeem and to restore the brokenness of this world that he is seated on his throne and we can trust him.

458
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:38,180
All right.

459
00:33:38,180 --> 00:33:39,740
Moving on.

460
00:33:39,740 --> 00:33:40,920
I really have to move fast.

461
00:33:40,920 --> 00:33:41,640
I promise I will.

462
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:42,000
All right.

463
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:45,020
Verse eight.

464
00:33:45,020 --> 00:33:51,240
After we see this plan that God is working with human beings to redeem human beings and to restore all of creation.

465
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:59,720
It says that the, the, the symbols that represent all of creation, they fall down on their faces and day and night they worship God.

466
00:33:59,880 --> 00:34:06,140
Holy, holy, holy, holy, holy is the Lord God almighty who was and who is and who is to come.

467
00:34:06,140 --> 00:34:07,340
They go on worthy.

468
00:34:07,340 --> 00:34:17,060
Are you our Lord and God to receive glory and honor and power for you created all things and by your will, they existed and were created.

469
00:34:17,060 --> 00:34:24,220
Again, hopefully, I hope that we can see how this unveiling of the present reality of heaven might encourage the faint.

470
00:34:24,960 --> 00:34:28,060
Who are being persecuted, who are being marginalized.

471
00:34:28,060 --> 00:34:37,020
John's saying no matter what persecution or suffering or anxiety or fear we might experience on earth, heaven is a real place.

472
00:34:37,020 --> 00:34:40,760
And God is seated on his throne.

473
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:44,560
Don't be afraid.

474
00:34:44,560 --> 00:34:48,440
Don't be afraid.

475
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:49,000
Okay.

476
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:50,940
We go on to verse five.

477
00:34:50,940 --> 00:34:52,400
This is all good news, right?

478
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:53,940
Lots of good news happening.

479
00:34:54,560 --> 00:34:59,480
God is, is, was, and always will be redeeming humanity, restoring all of creation.

480
00:34:59,480 --> 00:35:01,360
We can trust him even when we can't see it.

481
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:02,140
All good news.

482
00:35:02,140 --> 00:35:04,160
We get a little bit of bad news in chapter five.

483
00:35:04,160 --> 00:35:15,040
John then sees in the right hand of God seated on the throne, a scroll written on it, both in the back and sealed with seven seals.

484
00:35:15,040 --> 00:35:21,360
And I saw a mighty angel proclaiming with a loud voice, who is worthy to open the scroll and break its seals?

485
00:35:22,420 --> 00:35:29,220
And no one in heaven or on earth or under the scroll or to look into it.

486
00:35:29,220 --> 00:35:38,580
And so I began to open the scroll or to look into it.

487
00:35:40,020 --> 00:35:40,860
John's vision continues.

488
00:35:40,860 --> 00:35:41,480
John's vision continues.

489
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:46,420
And this scroll represents God's redemption plan for all of creation.

490
00:35:46,820 --> 00:35:52,700
From beginning to end, God has an eternal plan for how he is going to redeem humanity and restore all of creation.

491
00:35:52,700 --> 00:35:56,660
It's all written down and it's sealed and someone has to open it.

492
00:35:57,980 --> 00:35:59,740
And the question becomes who?

493
00:35:59,740 --> 00:36:00,720
Who can open it?

494
00:36:00,720 --> 00:36:03,860
Who can bring about the reconciliation of all human beings?

495
00:36:03,860 --> 00:36:05,200
Who is powerful enough?

496
00:36:05,200 --> 00:36:06,380
Who is wise enough?

497
00:36:06,380 --> 00:36:08,760
Who is humble enough in all of creation?

498
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:17,960
And John weeps because he knows from his experience and from his study of history that no one in all of creation is worthy to do that job.

499
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:26,960
And I think you and I intuitively know the same thing from our personal experience and from our study of history.

500
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:30,960
Think about the best leaders that you have ever been around.

501
00:36:30,960 --> 00:36:34,000
Think about the best leaders in human history that you have read about.

502
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:35,080
All of them.

503
00:36:36,500 --> 00:36:39,840
Our best and our brightest are flawed and selfish at the core.

504
00:36:39,840 --> 00:36:47,240
Even if you are extremely optimistic about your presidential candidate, you know that they are not worthy for a job like this.

505
00:36:47,240 --> 00:36:50,260
So we weep.

506
00:36:50,260 --> 00:36:54,700
Until we get to verse 5.

507
00:36:54,700 --> 00:36:57,440
And one of the elders said to me,

508
00:36:57,560 --> 00:36:59,260
Weep no more.

509
00:36:59,260 --> 00:37:06,480
Look or behold, the lion of the tribe of Judah, the root of David, has conquered so that he can open the scroll and its seven seals.

510
00:37:06,480 --> 00:37:13,860
And between the throne, the four living creatures, and among the elders, I saw a lamb.

511
00:37:13,860 --> 00:37:19,140
Symbolism that we even as New Testament Christians get.

512
00:37:19,540 --> 00:37:28,880
I saw a lamb standing as though it had been slain with seven horns and with seven eyes, which are the seven spirits of God, sent out into all the earth.

513
00:37:28,880 --> 00:37:33,720
And he went and he took the scroll from the right hand of him who was seated on the throne.

514
00:37:33,720 --> 00:37:40,440
And when he had taken the scroll, the four living creatures and the 24 elders fell down before the lamb.

515
00:37:40,440 --> 00:37:45,240
This is where it starts to get really, really good.

516
00:37:45,240 --> 00:37:47,120
And I didn't leave myself enough time to preach.

517
00:37:47,120 --> 00:37:49,100
So, sorry.

518
00:37:49,100 --> 00:37:58,700
Jesus, being both fully God and fully man, is the only one worthy to bring about God's plan of redemption.

519
00:37:58,700 --> 00:38:02,920
To redeem humanity and to restore creation.

520
00:38:02,920 --> 00:38:07,920
He is the only one that is worthy of us to put our trust in.

521
00:38:07,920 --> 00:38:14,440
And so if you're in here and you're putting your trust in any other person, in any other leader, in any other political party,

522
00:38:14,440 --> 00:38:18,120
whatever it might be, John is pulling back the curtains of heaven and saying,

523
00:38:18,120 --> 00:38:22,560
do not trust anyone other than the lamb who's been slain, for he is worthy.

524
00:38:22,560 --> 00:38:31,780
But the amazing, wonderful thing is that Jesus' victory does not come the way that we think it's supposed to come.

525
00:38:34,660 --> 00:38:42,160
John hears about the lion of Judah, the root of David, strength, power.

526
00:38:42,160 --> 00:38:43,820
That makes sense.

527
00:38:43,820 --> 00:38:51,680
But when he looks to see this lion, instead he sees a lamb that was slain.

528
00:38:53,060 --> 00:38:55,440
With seven horns and seven eyes.

529
00:38:55,440 --> 00:38:56,940
Again, fun symbolism, right?

530
00:38:56,940 --> 00:38:57,880
We all know what that means.

531
00:38:57,880 --> 00:39:01,520
Seven is the number of completion in Hebrew.

532
00:39:01,520 --> 00:39:06,680
And the horns are representing strength and the eyes are representing wisdom.

533
00:39:06,680 --> 00:39:13,660
What John is saying is that Jesus laying down his life in sacrificial love is the strength and wisdom of heaven.

534
00:39:16,140 --> 00:39:18,020
If you're following along in your notes, there you go.

535
00:39:18,020 --> 00:39:21,700
Sacrificial love is the strength and wisdom of God.

536
00:39:21,700 --> 00:39:26,500
The victory that Jesus has on the cross is not like the victory of this world.

537
00:39:26,500 --> 00:39:27,520
It doesn't make sense.

538
00:39:27,520 --> 00:39:33,000
To the wisdom of this world, our political parties lead with strength and power.

539
00:39:33,640 --> 00:39:35,780
And Jesus leads with sacrificial love.

540
00:39:35,780 --> 00:39:44,560
Again, we could see how this would be an encouragement to a persecuted group with no power or influence to speak of.

541
00:39:44,560 --> 00:39:49,760
John is telling the churches that he pastors through this vision, you will overcome.

542
00:39:49,760 --> 00:39:52,000
You will have victory.

543
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:55,380
You need only to follow the way of the lamb.

544
00:39:55,380 --> 00:40:00,220
What a timely message for us.

545
00:40:00,220 --> 00:40:02,540
In a time of confusion and discouragement,

546
00:40:02,540 --> 00:40:04,260
God is on the throne.

547
00:40:04,260 --> 00:40:08,140
The lamb who was slain is worthy to bring about God's plan of redemption.

548
00:40:08,140 --> 00:40:10,540
We don't need to be afraid.

549
00:40:10,540 --> 00:40:14,060
We don't need to lash out or fight back.

550
00:40:14,060 --> 00:40:16,700
We only need to follow the example of the lamb.

551
00:40:16,700 --> 00:40:22,220
Loving our enemies and praying for those who persecute us.

552
00:40:22,220 --> 00:40:27,380
This is the wisdom and strength of heaven and we will overcome.

553
00:40:32,540 --> 00:40:34,720
Revelation 5, verses 9 and 10.

554
00:40:34,720 --> 00:40:43,060
After the lamb who was slain takes the scroll and begins the plan of redemption for all creation,

555
00:40:43,060 --> 00:40:44,740
they sing a new song.

556
00:40:45,140 --> 00:40:55,900
Worthy are you to take the scroll to open its seals for you were slain and by your blood you ransomed people for God from every tribe and language and people and nation.

557
00:40:56,020 --> 00:41:01,960
And you have made them a kingdom of priests to our God and they shall reign on the earth.

558
00:41:01,960 --> 00:41:10,620
Taking notes, our response to all of this, to the realities of heaven, our response should be worship and participation.

559
00:41:12,420 --> 00:41:14,860
They fall down and they say, worthy are you.

560
00:41:14,860 --> 00:41:16,920
We should fall down and say, worthy are you.

561
00:41:16,920 --> 00:41:17,780
But look what it says.

562
00:41:17,780 --> 00:41:24,640
It says, you ransomed a people of God from every tribe, language, people, and nation and you made them a priest.

563
00:41:24,640 --> 00:41:25,780
Who is that talking about?

564
00:41:25,780 --> 00:41:27,940
The church.

565
00:41:27,940 --> 00:41:29,760
That's us.

566
00:41:29,760 --> 00:41:31,920
Jesus did this.

567
00:41:31,920 --> 00:41:34,340
He took the scroll.

568
00:41:34,340 --> 00:41:35,160
He opened the seals.

569
00:41:35,160 --> 00:41:44,200
He established a people of God from every language, tribe, nation, and tongue so that we can go about proclaiming his kingdom on earth as it is in heaven.

570
00:41:44,200 --> 00:41:49,040
And in order for us to do this, we've got to get heaven into our bones now.

571
00:41:49,040 --> 00:41:58,480
We've got to remember that Jesus is seated on his throne, that he is worthy, and that the principles of his kingdom are sacrificial love.

572
00:41:58,480 --> 00:42:01,640
This is how we go about being priests.

573
00:42:01,640 --> 00:42:03,960
This is how we go about overcoming.

574
00:42:04,220 --> 00:42:07,980
This is how we go about having peace in the midst of difficult circumstances.

575
00:42:07,980 --> 00:42:09,940
This is how we encourage the faint.

576
00:42:09,940 --> 00:42:12,940
Jesus, who was slain, is seated on the throne.

577
00:42:12,940 --> 00:42:16,840
Let's summarize both of these chapters this way.

578
00:42:16,840 --> 00:42:20,420
Look, the almighty God is seated on his throne.

579
00:42:20,420 --> 00:42:22,160
Don't be afraid.

580
00:42:22,160 --> 00:42:28,200
The slain lamb is worthy to bring about God's eternal plan of redemption and restoration.

581
00:42:28,200 --> 00:42:33,820
Citizens of heaven, take heart.

582
00:42:34,940 --> 00:42:35,840
Be encouraged.

583
00:42:35,840 --> 00:42:37,820
The lamb is overcome.

584
00:42:37,820 --> 00:42:40,780
We've had victory as one.

585
00:42:40,780 --> 00:42:41,980
It is secured.

586
00:42:41,980 --> 00:42:43,520
We might not see it.

587
00:42:43,520 --> 00:42:46,560
We might not experience it fully here on earth, but it is true.

588
00:42:46,560 --> 00:42:49,080
It is a truer reality than what we see with our eyes.

589
00:42:49,080 --> 00:42:55,360
If we would have faith, if we would walk by faith and not by sight, if we would get this reality into our bones.

590
00:42:56,620 --> 00:43:01,880
Imagine what God would do with a kingdom of priests who lived as if heaven's realities were true on earth.

591
00:43:03,880 --> 00:43:07,180
And if you're here and you don't know Jesus, you're not really sure where you're at with this whole thing.

592
00:43:07,260 --> 00:43:11,740
I was just having a conversation with somebody this morning who had a heck of a week.

593
00:43:12,740 --> 00:43:19,880
And she said to me what I've said to many others, and that is, I don't know how people who don't have Jesus do it.

594
00:43:20,920 --> 00:43:29,640
And so if you're in here and you don't know Jesus and you're discouraged and you're confused and you're angry and you're sad and you're whatever mix of emotions you're feeling right now.

595
00:43:32,640 --> 00:43:41,200
I believe that what John wrote down in the book of Revelation is a unveiling of what is true eternally in heaven.

596
00:43:41,200 --> 00:43:43,680
Jesus is on the throne.

597
00:43:43,680 --> 00:43:47,140
There's peace in the midst of your anxiety.

598
00:43:47,140 --> 00:43:49,800
There's victory in the midst of your defeat.

599
00:43:49,800 --> 00:43:53,860
There's salvation from the brokenness of this world.

600
00:43:54,280 --> 00:44:03,240
All you need to do is bow down at the feet of the Lamb and say, worthy are you to receive honor and glory and power and wisdom.

601
00:44:03,240 --> 00:44:08,020
If that's something that you want to do, I'd love to have a conversation with you about that.

602
00:44:08,020 --> 00:44:16,640
Everyone else, you are a kingdom of priests bought with the precious blood of Jesus.

603
00:44:16,640 --> 00:44:24,260
May you go out this week living on mission for the kingdom of God.

604
00:44:24,980 --> 00:44:27,860
Seeing the kingdom of God more visibly on earth as it is in heaven.

605
00:44:27,860 --> 00:44:32,400
Do it with sacrificial love and wisdom.

606
00:44:32,400 --> 00:44:33,120
Let's pray.

607
00:44:33,120 --> 00:44:34,760
Father, we love you.

608
00:44:34,760 --> 00:44:36,180
We thank you for Jesus.

609
00:44:36,180 --> 00:44:41,020
We thank you for this vision, this heavenly unveiling.

610
00:44:41,020 --> 00:44:46,460
God, we probably won't ever understand it fully or completely, but we get the gist.

611
00:44:46,460 --> 00:44:48,580
You're seated on your throne.

612
00:44:48,580 --> 00:44:52,480
You're bringing about the redemption of humanity and the restoration of all creation.

613
00:44:52,620 --> 00:44:57,880
And even though we can't see it, you are the God who was and is and is to come.

614
00:44:57,880 --> 00:45:04,860
And so because we've seen you do it in the past and you've promised to do it in the future,

615
00:45:04,860 --> 00:45:11,520
God, we are going to remain faithful and we are going to persevere because we trust that you are who you say you are.

616
00:45:11,520 --> 00:45:13,260
You'll do what you say you're going to do.

617
00:45:15,220 --> 00:45:17,660
Pray all of this in Jesus' name.

618
00:45:17,660 --> 00:45:18,680
Amen.

619
00:45:18,680 --> 00:45:22,060
Thank you, church.

620
00:45:22,060 --> 00:45:23,660
Spend time with one another.

621
00:45:23,660 --> 00:45:27,520
Greet one another with holy handshakes and hugs.

622
00:45:27,520 --> 00:45:29,500
Go in peace.

623
00:45:29,500 --> 00:45:58,160
Go in peace.
